## 1. Print Function

- `\n` adds a new line
- `\t` adds a tab
- Wrapping text in `"""..."""` lets a `print()` span multiple lines

```python
print("Your Learning Path:\n\t-Python Basics\n\t-Data Engineering\n\t-AI")

# Same thing, spread across lines with triple quotes
print("""Your Learning Path:

\t-Python Basics

\t-Data Engineering

\t-AI""")
```

