## 7. Numeric Functions

### Number types
- `int` — whole numbers: `5`, `-12`, `10000`
- `float` — decimals: `3.15`, `-0.5`, `100.00`
- `complex` — real + imaginary numbers (advanced math/engineering/physics)

### Reference
| Category | Functions |
|---|---|
| Type | `type()`, `int()`, `float()`, `complex()` |
| Math operators | `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `//`, `%`, `**` |
| Rounding | `abs()`, `round()`, `ceil()`, `floor()`, `trunc()` |
| Advanced math | `sqrt()`, `sin()`, `cos()`, `log()` |
| Random | `random()`, `randint()` |
| Validation | `.is_integer()`, `isinstance()` |

